{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"unfeared-camlet-hellbender","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Context / Problem\n\nA linked worktree's editable install records the project version in its `.dist-info`\nat install time. Rebasing that worktree onto a `main` that bumped the version does\n**not** refresh it, so `importlib.metadata.version(\"nava-rebar\")` keeps returning the\nold value while `pyproject.toml` says the new one.\n\nNothing warns. The mismatch surfaces only as a public-API-surface drift failure\nroughly 40 minutes into `make verify`, whose message names the baseline and tells\nyou to regenerate it — the opposite of the correct action. Following that advice\nwould commit a corrupted `tests/unit/api_surface_baseline.json`.\n\nThis cost one full 42-minute `make verify` run on story `19ba-bd62-1adb-41df` on\n2026-10-30, and the same trap was caught pre-emptively on `a018-a2c0-fc15-434c`\nminutes later, so it is not a one-off.\n\n## Observation (measured)\n\nIn `.rebar/worktrees/impl-19ba` after rebasing onto a `main` carrying 0.13.1 -> 0.14.0:\n\n- `pyproject.toml` declared `version = \"0.14.0\"`.\n- `.venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/nava_rebar-0.13.1.dist-info` was still present,\n  and `python -c 'import rebar; print(rebar.__version__)'` printed `0.13.1`.\n- `src/rebar/__init__.py:144` sets `__version__ = importlib.metadata.version(\"nava-rebar\")`,\n  so the stale dist-info is read straight into the public surface.\n- `make verify` failed with, verbatim:\n\n      Public API surface drift detected against the committed baseline\n      (tests/unit/api_surface_baseline.json):\n        ~ CHANGED  rebar.__version__\n      If this change is intentional, refresh the baseline and review the diff:\n          python scripts/gen_api_surface.py --update\n\n  from `tests/unit/test_api_surface_gate.py:78` and `:83`\n  (`test_committed_baseline_matches_live_surface`, `test_default_invocation_runs_the_check`).\n- Two further failures in the same run cleared on the rerun and are **not** attributed\n  here: `test_pytest_interleaved_conftest_args.py::test_conftest_fixtures_survive_a_parent_dir_file_arg_between_package_args`\n  and `test_mcp_entrypoint_provisioning.py::test_a_peer_finishing_the_clone_while_we_wait_skips_the_redundant_reclone`.\n  Their failure output does not name a version, so their cause is unestablished.\n- `make install` in the worktree replaced the dist-info with `nava_rebar-0.14.0` and the\n  rerun was clean: 20,087 passed, 28 skipped, 0 failures.\n\nThe distribution name is `nava-rebar`, not `rebar`; a probe written as\n`importlib.metadata.version(\"rebar\")` raises `PackageNotFoundError` in every worktree\nand silently proves nothing. That misnaming is itself an easy way to miss this.\n\n## Approach (direction, not a committed design)\n\nDetect the mismatch and fail fast with an actionable message instead of letting it\nreach the surface gate 40 minutes in. Compare the installed distribution version with\nthe version declared in `pyproject.toml` at session start, and when they differ say so\nand name the fix (`make install`) rather than the baseline. The surface-gate message\nshould also stop recommending `--update` when the only drift is `rebar.__version__`\nand the installed version disagrees with the tree, because regenerating the baseline\nthere commits the corruption.\n\n`AGENTS.md` should state the rule directly: run `make install` after any rebase that\ncrosses a version bump.\n\n## Scope\n\n- The check's home and the surface-gate message wording are for the implementer to\n  determine; this ticket does not pin them.\n- `AGENTS.md` — one line in the worktree/rebase guidance.\n- Tests covering both the mismatch and the aligned case.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] AC1: In a worktree whose installed `nava-rebar` dist-info version differs from the\n      `version` in `pyproject.toml`, the mismatch is reported with a message naming both\n      versions and `make install` as the remedy, before the public-API surface gate runs.\n- [ ] AC2: When the installed version matches `pyproject.toml`, no such message is\n      emitted and no existing behaviour changes.\n- [ ] AC3: When the only public-API surface drift is `rebar.__version__` and the installed\n      version disagrees with `pyproject.toml`, the surface-gate failure text does **not**\n      recommend `python scripts/gen_api_surface.py --update`.\n- [ ] AC4: `AGENTS.md` states that `make install` must be run after a rebase that crosses\n      a version bump; verified by grep.\n- [ ] AC5: New tests cover AC1, AC2 and AC3 and are red before the fix.\n- [ ] AC6: `make verify` exits 0, and the Gerrit change carries `LLM-Review +1` and\n      `Verified +1`.","id":"9cee-46d4-a822-43c0","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Worktree venv keeps stale dist-info after a rebase across a version bump"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1793420835776327731,"uuid":"ee8d2267-a319-414a-9652-6b272d3efb44"}